# tuned/repo.env -- NCCL-specific settings for tuned builds. Sourced by tuned/env.sh
# after the shared device and toolkit definitions (tuned/common-data, from
# zbrad/tuned-common). Tracked, so a release is reproducible.
#
# This file may only ADD repo-specific settings. Changing any shared key
# (GPU_TUNED_*, CUDA_*, TOOLKIT_*) is a loud error from env.sh.
#
# Plain assignment on purpose: this file is sourced inside a function, where
# `declare` would make the variable local and lose it.

# What this build is based on: an upstream NVIDIA/nccl release TAG, not a branch. This branch builds for CUDA 13.3 and is based on
# v2.31.2-1, the newest NCCL release NVIDIA ships for the cuda13.3 flavour (apt libnccl2 2.31.2-1+cuda13.3; the other 13.3 flavour is
# 2.30.7). One branch per toolkit, tuned-builds-<cuda>, each based on the release NVIDIA ships for that toolkit; if we ever need a fix
# for one, the base is that tag. Used by the build-info stamp and checked by tuned/release.sh.
GPU_TUNED_UPSTREAM_REF="v2.31.2-1"

# Strings the fork keeps in upstream-owned files. tools/upstream-sync.sh refuses a merge
# that loses one. The first is the marker of the arch-gate fix in src/device/Makefile
# (NVIDIA/nccl issue 2420: LDMC FP8 kernels ignored the caller's NVCC_GENCODE).
GPU_TUNED_FORK_MARKERS="zbrad/nccl tuned-builds: compile LDMC"
